        "original_id": "6d157fb0-402e-5815-a3f4-afc0e6b530c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Don Giovanni, Cardillac\n- People: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Lorenzo Da Ponte, Paul Hindemith, Maria de Francesca-Cavazza, Wolfgang Sawallisch\n- Products: Deutsche Grammophon Munich DVD\n- Topics: Marzemino\n\nFacts:\n- Don Giovanni is an opera in two acts with music by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart and an Italian libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte.\n- Don Giovanni has the complete title \"Il dissoluto punito, ossia il Don Giovanni,\" meaning \"The Rake Punished, namely Don Giovanni\" or \"The Libertine Punished.\"\n- Cardillac is an opera by Paul Hindemith in three acts and four scenes.\n- Marzemino is especially noted for being mentioned in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera Don Giovanni.\n- In a 1985 Munich DVD issued by Deutsche Grammophon, Maria de Francesca-Cavazza appears as Cardillac's daughter in Paul Hindemith's opera Cardillac.\n- The 1985 Munich DVD of Cardillac featuring Maria de Francesca-Cavazza was conducted by Wolfgang Sawallisch.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
